{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MP6CaJaJrmA8K5iYLfC5cP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EFRhoLrAUDcLZKLTPvByMN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# Task: Batch Round 0 Coset-Parallel Kernel Launches\n\nTask name: 2026-04-10-2049-batch-round0-coset-parallel\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nRound 0 of constraint evaluation is the worst-scaling component in STARK excl trace: 570ms at APC 300 vs 174ms at APC 0 (3.28x increase), despite total constraint instances *decreasing* by 2.23x. This inverse scaling accounts for +396ms of overhead and is the single largest contributor preventing STARK excl trace from scaling with workload reduction.\n\n**Root cause: GPU SM underutilization.** Nsight profiling shows Round 0 at APC 300 launches ~935 `coset_parallel` kernels (539 zerocheck + 396 logup), each processing a single small AIR instance. These kernels have tiny grids (3-12 thread blocks) on a GPU with 108+ SMs, resulting in 3-11% SM utilization per kernel. The kernels execute sequentially on a single CUDA stream, so the GPU processes them one after another, wasting 89-97% of its compute capacity on each launch.\n\nProfiling breakdown at APC 300:\n- `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel<true,false>`: 220ms, 539 instances (avg 408us, median 275us)\n- `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel<true,false>`: 195ms, 396 instances (avg 493us, median 378us)\n- `*_coset_parallel_kernel<false,false>` variants: 49ms combined, 535 instances\n- Total coset_parallel GPU time: **~464ms** (81% of Round 0's 570ms wall clock)\n- Non-coset-parallel kernels (larger AIRs): ~96ms\n- Phase 2 CPU processing: ~10ms\n\nAt APC 0, coset_parallel kernels total only ~60ms (137+small instances) because there are only 99 AIR instances with larger traces that better utilize the GPU.\n\n## Proposed Approach\n\nBatch multiple small AIR instances into single kernel launches using a per-AIR metadata approach. This follows the same pattern that successfully optimized Stacked Reduction (task 2026-04-10-2145-batch-degenerate-stacked-reduction), which achieved 2.1x improvement by batching ~10,348 degenerate window launches into single kernel launches.\n\n**Mechanism:** For each coset_parallel kernel (zerocheck and logup):\n\n1. **Classify** AIR instances into coset_parallel-eligible (small) vs non-coset-parallel (large), using the existing `COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768`.\n\n2. **Create per-AIR metadata struct** containing: pointers to trace data, constraint bytecodes (`d_rules`), selectors, eq values, public values, lambda powers; plus scalar parameters (skip_domain, num_x, height, num_cosets, g_shift). Upload metadata array to GPU via single H2D copy.\n\n3. **Launch batched kernel** with grid dimensions `(max_x_blocks, max_num_cosets, num_airs_in_batch)`. Each AIR's thread blocks are identified by `blockIdx.z`. Each block loads its AIR's metadata and evaluates constraints independently, exactly as the current single-AIR kernel does.\n\n4. **Batched reduction**: Use the existing `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` in `sumcheck.cuh:261-291`, which already supports segment offsets for multi-AIR reduction.\n\n5. **Non-coset-parallel AIRs** continue using the existing per-AIR kernel path (these are already well-utilizing the GPU).\n\nThe batched kernel code would be structurally identical to the existing coset_parallel kernels, with the addition of `blockIdx.z` indexing into the metadata array and bounds-checking for AIRs with fewer x_blocks or cosets than the grid maximum.\n\n## Expected Outcome\n\n- **Round 0 APC 300**: Reduce from 570ms to ~250-350ms (150-300ms savings). The coset_parallel portion should improve 2-4x from better SM utilization.\n- **STARK excl trace APC 300**: Reduce from 2205ms to ~1905-2055ms (7-14% improvement vs current, 15-22% vs baseline).\n- **Scaling ratio** (APC 300 / APC 0): Improve from 1.027 toward ~0.90 or lower.\n- **APC 0**: Negligible change (only 99 instances, most already use non-coset-parallel path).\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n1. **Primary**: Round 0 APC 300 wall time < 400ms (currently 570ms, target >30% reduction).\n2. **Secondary**: STARK excl trace APC 300 < 2050ms (currently 2205ms, target >7% reduction).\n3. **Scaling**: STARK excl trace APC 300 / APC 0 ratio < 0.97 (currently 1.027).\n4. **Correctness**: All 94 `openvm-cuda-backend` tests pass. Proof verification succeeds for APC 0/100/300.\n\n## Considered Alternatives\n\n1. **Rayon-parallelize Round 0 Phase 2 CPU processing** (estimated 10ms savings). Phase 2 at APC 300 is only ~10ms (the Phase 1 deferred-sync optimization made GPU execution the bottleneck). Too small an improvement to justify as a standalone task.\n\n2. **Multi-stream Round 0 (launch per-AIR kernels on N CUDA streams)** (estimated 100-200ms). Achieves better GPU utilization without new kernel code. However, requires refactoring the single-stream architecture, per-stream temp buffer allocation (higher memory), and doesn't eliminate per-kernel CPU launch overhead. Batched kernel approach is more efficient and follows the proven pattern.\n\n3. **Batch LogUp GKR input evaluation kernels** (estimated 100-250ms). The `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel` totals 427ms at APC 300 with 791 instances. Batching could improve scaling, but the GKR protocol's sequential layer dependencies limit how much can be parallelized. Round 0 has a larger absolute improvement potential and is fully parallelizable.\n\n4. **Batch non-degenerate stacked reduction kernels** (estimated 70-86ms). Still has 7467 per-window kernel launches contributing ~86ms of CPU overhead. Moderate impact but smaller than Round 0 batching. Good follow-up target.\n\n5. **Cache `calculate_zero_hash` results** (initially estimated ~100ms, but determined to be outside STARK excl trace — this kernel is in the openvm VM memory Merkle tree, part of Set Initial Memory phase, not the proving phase). Ruled out as out of scope.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":336,"cache_read_input_tokens":106606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":336},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c7f624f-3476-4fc9-b97f-853499dc45e9","uuid":"ea1ad5c2-8737-48f6-a9da-28743a594c22"}
